File Naming and Batch Detection Guidelines

File Naming for 2D vs 3D Images
SampleName_Markers_(optional:3D)_(optional:Location).tif

2D images:
SampleName_Markers.tif
3D z-stacks:
SampleName_Markers_3D_location.tif

The pipeline will automatically detect 3D images if the filename contains 3D (case-insensitive) before the file extension.

If present, the location tag (e.g., SampleName_Markers_3D_Location1.tif) indicates a zoomed-in region, often for 3D images.
The pipeline will use the corresponding 2D files (with the same sample name and markers, but without the location tag) as the reference for each 3D location.
If no location tag is present, the file is assumed to cover the whole sample.


Batch Detection
A "batch" is defined as a set of files with different sample names (the part before the first underscore).
If all files share the same sample name, the pipeline will treat them as a single sample (not a batch).
Please follow these conventions to ensure correct processing.